Line 13: "first's next" could be nothing, so check it first.
    say first's next's value.
        ^^^^^^^^^^^^
Use it inside "if first's next is not nothing:".

Line 14: This is a node or nothing, so check it first.
    say (find with 1 and first)'s value.
        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Give it a name with "let", then use it inside "if NAME is not nothing:".

Line 15: "value" needs a node for "start", but this is a node or nothing.
    say value with first's next.
                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^
It could be nothing. Check it first, like "if first's next is not nothing:".

Line 16: "first" is a node, so it's never nothing.
    if first is nothing, say "never".
       ^^^^^
Only a value that's "a node or nothing" can be nothing.

Line 17: I can't compare a number with nothing.
    if 5 is not nothing, say "never".
       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Only a value whose kind ends in "or nothing" can be nothing, like a field or input that's "a number or nothing".

Line 18: I can't compare nothing with nothing.
    if nothing is nothing, say "always".
       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Compare something that can be nothing with it, like "if the node's next is nothing".

Line 20: "first" is a node (made on line 12), but this is a node or nothing.
    set first to later.
                 ^^^^^
A name keeps the kind of value it was made with. To keep a node or nothing, make a new name for it.

Line 21: The field "value" is a number, but this is nothing.
    set first's value to nothing.
                         ^^^^^^^

Line 24: This can be nothing, but it's used as a list of numbers here, which can't be.
        if x is not nothing, give back item 1 of x.
                                                 ^
Only a number, text, a yes/no value, a record or a kind with variants can be nothing. To say a list or map has nothing in it, make it empty.

Line 31: "later" could be nothing, so check it first.
        say later's value.
            ^^^^^
Use it inside "if later is not nothing:".

Line 35: "walker" could be nothing, so check it first.
            say walker's value.
                ^^^^^^
Use it inside "if walker is not nothing:".
